{
  "id": "Compound::DB00492 - Disease::DOID:10763",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Fosinopril may be related to Hypertension (disease) through a series of interconnected pathways. Fosinopril is linked to Oligohydramnios and Skull Hypoplasia, both of which are conditions that can be treated with Captopril, an Ace Inhibitor and L-Proline Derivative. Captopril, in turn, is used to treat Hypertension, indicating a potential therapeutic relationship. The evidence also shows that Fosinopril is associated with Swelling Of Limb, which is treated with Irbesartan, another antihypertensive agent. These pathways collectively suggest that Fosinopril may exert a role in the pathophysiology of Hypertension through its effects on various physiological processes, potentially influencing blood pressure regulation. The integration of these relationships highlights the complex interplay between Fosinopril and antihypertensive mechanisms, though the exact nature of the causal relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
